- Follow the standard project structure:
```
src/
├── app/
│   ├── (private)/     # Protected routes requiring authentication
│   └── (public)/      # Public routes
├── actions/           # Server actions
├── lib/
│   ├── data/         # Data layer
│   │   ├── dal/      # Data Access Layer
│   │   └── dto/      # Data Transfer Objects
│   ├── definitions/  # TypeScript definitions
│   └── models/       # Database models
└── components/       # React components
```

- Place components in appropriate directories based on their scope
- Keep related files together in feature-based directories
- Use clear, descriptive names for directories and files
- Follow the naming conventions for each file type
